Z||000000||penetrator||05-20-2001||06:49 PM||||hi<BR>I recently discoverd a rattleing noise somewhere in the back of the car when i was brakeing with the engine (motorbrake). And the sound was(is) really loud and sounds really bad, like there is some Titan Rocks in the gearbox. <BR>First i was worried and did't want to drive the car til i knew what was wrong. But after a day or so i tried to drive again, and the noise was gone, but not for long, it started again after i was driven a long trip and was going to gear down to the 3rd gear (4-speed) then the ratteling noise was back, clearer and louder. <BR>But today i discoverd that my polybushings in the dogbone was scratched as the engine have been moving forward/backwards. So i tighten the bolt real hard and tried to drive again but the sound was constant. But my patience was over and i wanted to know wich part on the car was going to be broke, so i put the pedeal in the metal and released the clutch and was expecting the gearbox to explode or something, but luckly i was going away in high speed with a wheelspin. But after that the noise was gone?<BR>Could the reason be that the dogbone was loose and was fixed in its right postition again after my little "experiment" ?<P>Someone else that had this rattling noise?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||penetrator||05-21-2001||07:56 AM||||Anyone? ||||reg||10
